{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And the reason for <b>your brothers, the children of Esau</b>: that the kinship of Israel is from Abraham, and all his seed are brothers, for all of them are circumcised. And this is the reason for 'You shall not abominate an Edomite, for he is your brother' (Deuteronomy 23:8). Only the sons of the concubines — Ishmael, Midian, and all the children of Keturah — are not included in brotherhood, from what is written: 'For in Isaac shall seed be called to you' (Genesis 21:12)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:15.771950717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}